e number have to be  divisible by four  we also know that the first digit has to  be odd but it is not the digit 5 which  is already used  so which two digit numbers satisfy this  property  we can start counting up from 0 and look  for two digit numbers that are multiples  of 4 with this property there are only 8  cases to consider  and there's a pattern in these cases  the last digit of the number is either a  2 or a 6  so that means  this tangent number must have the fourth  digit equal to two or six  we'll write out two different  possibilities  now we're going to figure out the six  digit  we know that the first three digits are  divisible by three so that means the sum  of the first three digits is a multiple  of three  the first six digits must be divisible  by six that means they must also be  divisible by three and therefore the  first six digits must also have a sum  that's a multiple of three  now since the first three digits have a  sum that's a multiple of three this can  only happen if also the fourth fifth and  sixth digits also have a sum that's a  multiple of three  so let's consider the fourth fifth and  sixth digit if we have two plus five  that gets us to seven  now we need to use one of the even  numbers that's remaining to get to a  multiple of three  we can't use four or six  but the number eight would work seven  plus eight is fifteen which is a  multiple of three  six plus five is equal to eleven  we need to use one of the remaining even  numbers to get to a multiple of three  we can similarly conclude this digit  would have to be four  now let's consider the first eight  digits of the number  this needs to be divisible by eight  which means the last three digits have  to be divisible by eight  so we wanna look at numbers in the eight  hundreds and the four hundreds we also  know that the middle digit has to be odd  but not equal to five  and we can't use one of the even numbers  we've already used  so we could start counting from 800 and  go up multiples of eight  see which numbers satisfy this property  we do the same thing for the 400s  there are only a few cases  that could possibly have  an odd number in the middle and it  doesn't use one of the even numbers  that's already remaining  in the case of the 800s we've we can't  have 832 or 872 because we've already  used the number two in two five eight  so we remove a couple possibilities  there similarly for the four hundreds we  have to remove the digit 6 because 654  already uses the digit 6.  so this leaves us with two numbers in  the 800s and two numbers in the 400s  so we put those in we have four total  possibilities for a number so we've  actually filled in a lot of digits of  this number  we didn't fill in one more digit  we have exactly one even number that's  remaining  this has to be the last even digit  in the first two cases that'll be four  and in the last two cases that'll be  eight  now we have exactly three digits  remaining in our number  these will be odd digits in the first  case it'll be 379 then 137 then 179 and  finally one three nine  so how can we reduce the number of  possibilities further well we need the  first three digits to be divisible by  three so the sum of the first three  digits has to be a multiple of three  if we look at our first case we have  something for something and we need to  have three seven or nine in these places  we can try to figure out sums which have  four in the middle that'll get us to a  multiple of three  none of these are going to work so this  entire case can be removed we will never  get something that will satisfy the  property we want  let's look at the next case  we have 1 3 and 7 and 4 in the middle  so 1 plus 4 plus 7 is equal to 12 which  is a multiple of 3. so we could have 147  or 741.  we'll do the same thing for the next  case we have the digits 1 7 and 9.  now there are a couple of sums that get  us to a multiple three so that leads to  four different possibilities for the  numbers  the final case is similar there are two  possibilities to get to multiple three  which leads to four different cases  so we have 4 plus 4 plus 2 which is a  total of 10 different numbers  so we've reduced this from over 3  million numbers to check and there are  only 10 possible numbers that this could  be  now which number is the answer well we  still need the first seven digits to be  divisible by seven so you could check  the first seven digits divided by seven  see which one's divisible and there's  only one number that works  this is three billion eight hundred and  sixteen million 547  290 and that's our answer  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on facebook google plus and  patreon you can catch me on social media  at preshtalwalker and like this video  please check out my books there are  links in the video description

